{%- doc -%}
  Renders a product's price as a Mionas text role, with an optional struck-through compare-at price.

  @param {product} [closest.product] - The product whose price to render. Renders nothing if absent.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The product price as a Mionas text role. Replaces blocks/mionas-product-price.liquid, which did the
  same job but restated --text-role-body-md-* by hand instead of spending the role vocabulary, and so
  could not follow it when a role changed.

  Renders through snippets/mionas-text.liquid, the same snippet blocks/mionas-text.liquid renders,
  so size, line-height, letter-spacing, family and colour are the role's. Only the weight is the
  price's own -- see the stylesheet.

  VARIANT AND SIZE ARE EXACTLY blocks/mionas-text.liquid's band x size grid, no more -- split into
  the same two settings, 1:1 with Text.tsx's own `variant`/`size` props, for the same reason and at
  the same time mionas-text's combined Role select was split. Color was renamed from `variant` to
  `color` for the same reason it was there: the new band setting needed the id `variant`, and a
  Shopify block schema cannot have two settings share one id. It used to carry a sixteenth option,
  Stamp, which is not a Text role at all but a component of its own
  (../design-system/src/react/Stamp/Stamp.tsx, mirrored here as blocks/mionas-stamp.liquid) -- a
  price is Text, so it cannot offer it. That also matches ProductCard.module.css, whose `.price`
  declares a weight and a colour and nothing else: the price inherits Text's own face rather than
  Stamp's Oswald. The three settings sites that had selected it moved to label-lg, the role Stamp
  itself renders at, so the figures kept their size and dropped only the uppercase Oswald.

  WHY A DEDICATED BLOCK RATHER THAN JUST USING blocks/mionas-text.liquid:
  mionas-text takes literal copy from a richtext setting. A price is not literal copy -- it needs
  `| money` in the shop's currency and format, the compare-at comparison, and the accessible label on
  the struck-through original. And the product card renders ONE composition that every product in
  the grid reuses (a single fixed block id -- see sections/mionas-collection.liquid and Horizon's
  sections/main-collection.liquid), so a literal string would print the same figure on every card.
  That is the whole reason this exists as its own block.

  NOT IN THE DESIGN SYSTEM AS A STANDALONE COMPONENT. ../design-system/src/react/ has Text and
  ProductCard/ProductCardPrice, but no Price -- so the tokens below are ProductCardPrice's while the
  role plumbing is Text's. Worth proposing back to ../design-system as a real component; that is a
  decision for its own repo, not something to assume from here.

  Reads closest.product, so it renders only inside a product context -- the card slot of
  sections/mionas-collection.liquid, a native product card, or a product page.

  The compare-at price is opt-in and off by default, carried over from mionas-product-price:
  ProductCardPrice.tsx shows a single price, but a bakery running a promotion has nowhere else to show
  the original on a card. It renders only when the product is genuinely discounted.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product = closest.product
  assign block_settings = block.settings

  assign on_sale = false
  if product.compare_at_price > product.price
    assign on_sale = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if product != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    comment
      Built as a string and handed to the snippet as `content`, which the snippet outputs unfiltered.
      Everything concatenated here is either `| money` output or a translated string, so there is no
      merchant-authored HTML in it.
    endcomment
    capture price_content
      echo '<span class="mionas-price__current">'
      echo product.price | money
      echo '</span>'

      if block_settings.show_compare_at_price and on_sale
        echo '<s class="mionas-price__compare">'
        echo '<span class="visually-hidden">'
        echo 'content.price_regular' | t
        echo '&nbsp;</span>'
        echo product.compare_at_price | money
        echo '</s>'
      endif
    endcapture
  -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    `spacing-style` is Horizon's own class (base.css:1352-1381): it turns the four --padding-*
    custom properties the snippet writes into real padding, with 0px fallbacks, and scales anything
    above 20px responsively. Same mechanism blocks/mionas-add-to-cart.liquid uses in this card.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture price_style -%}
    {%- render 'spacing-style', settings: block_settings -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- render 'mionas-text',
    content: price_content,
    variant: block_settings.variant,
    size: block_settings.size,
    color: block_settings.color,
    tag: 'p',
    class: 'mionas-price spacing-style',
    style: price_style,
    shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes
  -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /* The role owns size, line-height, letter-spacing, family and colour. Two things are left.

     display/align-items/gap, because the price is a row of two figures when a compare-at is shown,
     and the role vocabulary styles a single text node.

     And the weight: --product-card-price-font-weight, not the role's. The design system gives
     ProductCardPrice a weight token of its own because the price is 600 whatever size it is set at.

     COLOUR IS DELIBERATELY NOT OVERRIDDEN, unlike the block this replaces.
     --product-card-price-foreground references {text-color.default} in the design system's own token
     manifest, which is exactly what .text-role--default applies -- so spending it here would be a
     second name for the same value AND would make the Color setting below do nothing.

     NO PADDING IS DECLARED HERE ON PURPOSE. This used to carry
     padding-inline: var(--product-card-base-padding-inline), mirroring ProductCard.module.css, where
     the card has no padding of its own and each subcomponent insets itself. It is gone: padding is
     now four range settings rendered through snippets/spacing-style.liquid, defaulting to 0, so the
     block imposes no inset of its own and the composition decides. Same mechanism, same four setting
     ids, as blocks/mionas-add-to-cart.liquid and Horizon's own blocks/_product-card.liquid.

     The horizontal inset the card still needs is therefore set per instance in the theme editor:
     templates/index.json, templates/collection.json and the preset in sections/mionas-collection.liquid
     all configure padding-inline-start/end to 16 here, matching the product-title block beside it, so
     the price does not run to the card's edges. Nothing needs re-adding in CSS to keep that look.

     Note --product-card-base-padding-inline is consequently unspent theme-wide now: the only other
     block that still declared it, blocks/mionas-product-description.liquid, has been deleted. The
     token stays in assets/design-tokens.css because the design system still defines it.

     THE SELECTOR IS TWO CLASSES DEEP ON PURPOSE: every .text-role--<role> declares font-weight from a
     single-class selector in this same compiled stylesheet, so equal specificity would leave the
     winner to bundle order. .text-role.mionas-price is (0,2,0). Do not flatten it.

     It does NOT need to be two deep for the padding, and deliberately does not restate it: no
     .text-role rule declares padding at all, so `spacing-style`'s (0,1,0) padding in base.css has
     nothing in this bundle to lose source order to. */
  .text-role.mionas-price {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    font-weight: var(--product-card-price-font-weight);
  }

  /* Carried over from mionas-product-price: the struck-through original is deliberately the price
     colour at reduced opacity rather than a colour of its own, because the design system has no
     compare-at token. That keeps it on-palette whatever the Color setting resolves to -- which is now
     a merchant choice, so a hardcoded grey would have been wrong in more cases than before. */
  .mionas-price__compare {
    opacity: 0.6;
    font-weight: var(--text-role-body-md-font-weight, 400);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Mionas: Price",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "variant",
      "label": "Variant",
      "options": [
        { "value": "display", "label": "Display" },
        { "value": "headline", "label": "Headline" },
        { "value": "title", "label": "Title" },
        { "value": "body", "label": "Body" },
        { "value": "label", "label": "Label" }
      ],
      "default": "body",
      "info": "The same text variants as Mionas: Text. The price keeps its own weight."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "size",
      "label": "Size",
      "options": [
        { "value": "lg", "label": "Large" },
        { "value": "md", "label": "Medium" },
        { "value": "sm", "label": "Small" }
      ],
      "default": "md",
      "info": "The step within the Variant band."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "color",
      "label": "Color",
      "options": [
        { "value": "default", "label": "Default" },
        { "value": "primary", "label": "Primary" },
        { "value": "inverse-primary", "label": "Inverse primary" },
        { "value": "inverse-primary-muted", "label": "Inverse primary (muted)" },
        { "value": "accent", "label": "Accent" },
        { "value": "accent-inverse", "label": "Accent (inverse)" },
        { "value": "tint", "label": "Tint" }
      ],
      "default": "default"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_compare_at_price",
      "label": "Show compare-at price",
      "default": false,
      "info": "Shows the original price struck through, only on products that are actually discounted."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "t:settings.top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "t:settings.bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-start",
      "label": "t:settings.left",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-inline-end",
      "label": "t:settings.right",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Mionas: Price",
      "category": "t:categories.product"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
